-- smucclaw/l4-ide#1081, found by an independent re-check: doing `t` does NOT
-- remove the cure of t's lapse, because t's continuation holds another norm
-- with the same deadline (4, fixed) and the same cure. `t` at 3 starts U's
-- deadline of 11 (14); then t2's lapse at 4 arms Q's 10 after it (14): U and Q
-- tie. K's deadline (20) prints differently at every clock, so `t` at 0..4
-- reach different states and no merge hides the tie: what is left is whether
-- `t` is tried at 3. It is: the instants a lapse arms are tried for the act
-- whose own lapse arms them, and only a chain of acts is kept off them.
IMPORT prelude
DECLARE Person IS ONE OF T, U, Q, K
DECLARE Action IS ONE OF t, t2, u, q, k

GIVETH A DEONTIC Person Action
cure MEANS PARTY Q MUST q WITHIN 10 HENCE FULFILLED LEST BREACH BY Q

GIVETH A DEONTIC Person Action
succ2 MEANS
       (PARTY T MUST t WITHIN 4 OF 0
          HENCE (     (PARTY T MUST t2 WITHIN 4 OF 0 HENCE FULFILLED LEST cure)
                 RAND (PARTY U MUST u WITHIN 11 HENCE FULFILLED LEST BREACH BY U))
          LEST cure)
  RAND (PARTY K MUST k WITHIN 20 HENCE FULFILLED LEST BREACH BY K)

#TRACE succ2 AT 0 WITH
  PARTY T DOES t AT 3
  (WAITUNTIL 5)
